## Authentication

{{#eq auth "none"}}
No authentication is configured for this project.
{{/eq}}

{{#or (eq auth "jwt") (eq auth "jwt-refresh")}}
This project uses **JWT Bearer token** authentication.

### How to authenticate

1. Call `POST /api/v1/auth/login` to get an access token
2. Include the token in all protected requests:

```
Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
```

### Route protection

- All routes are **protected by default** via a global `JwtAuthGuard`
- Mark a route as public with the `@Public()` decorator
- Access the current user in any controller with `@CurrentUser()`

```typescript
// Public route — no token needed
@Public()
@Get('public-info')
getPublicInfo() { ... }

// Protected route — token required
@Get('private-data')
getPrivateData(@CurrentUser() user: { id: string; email: string }) { ... }
```

{{#eq auth "jwt-refresh"}}
### Token rotation

| Token | TTL | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Access token | `15m` | Send in `Authorization` header |
| Refresh token | `7d` | Send to `POST /auth/refresh` to get new pair |

When the access token expires, call `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh` with the refresh token in the `Authorization` header to receive a new token pair.
{{/eq}}
{{/or}}

{{#eq auth "api-key"}}
This project uses **API Key** authentication.

Send the key in every request header:
```
x-api-key: <your-api-key>
```
The key is configured via the `API_KEY` environment variable.
{{/eq}}

