## Database & Migrations

{{#eq orm "typeorm"}}
### TypeORM

```bash
# Run all pending migrations
make migrate

# Generate a new migration (after changing entities)
make migrate-gen name=AddUserRoles

# Revert last migration
make migrate-revert

# Seed the database
make seed
```

Migrations live in `src/database/migrations/`.
Entities are auto-discovered from `**/*.entity.ts` files.
{{/eq}}

{{#eq orm "prisma"}}
### Prisma

```bash
# Create and apply a new migration (development)
make migrate

# Apply migrations in production (no prompt)
make migrate-prod

# Open Prisma Studio (visual DB browser)
make studio

# Seed the database
make seed
```

Schema lives in `prisma/schema.prisma`.
After changing the schema, always run `make migrate` to keep the DB in sync.
{{/eq}}

{{#eq orm "drizzle"}}
### Drizzle ORM

```bash
# Generate migration files from schema changes
make migrate-gen

# Apply pending migrations
make migrate

# Open Drizzle Studio (visual DB browser)
make studio

# Seed the database
make seed
```

Schema lives in `src/database/schema.ts`.
Config lives in `drizzle.config.ts`.
{{/eq}}

{{#eq orm "mongoose"}}
### Mongoose

MongoDB with Mongoose — schema-first approach.
Schemas live alongside their modules in `*.schema.ts` files.
No migration step required — MongoDB is schemaless.
{{/eq}}

