## CI/CD Pipeline

GitHub Actions workflow at `.github/workflows/dev.yml`.

**Trigger:** Push to `main` branch

**Steps:**
1. Checkout code
2. Install Node.js 22
3. Install dependencies
4. Run linter
{{#eq testing "unit"}}
5. Run unit tests
6. Archive `node_modules`
7. Build (`npm run build`)
8. Archive `dist/`
9. SCP build to EC2 `~/builds`
10. SCP node_modules to EC2 `~/modules`
11. SSH into EC2 and run `./deploy.sh`
{{/eq}}
{{#eq testing "unit-e2e"}}
5. Run unit tests
6. Run E2E tests
7. Archive `node_modules`
8. Build (`npm run build`)
9. Archive `dist/`
10. SCP build to EC2 `~/builds`
11. SCP node_modules to EC2 `~/modules`
12. SSH into EC2 and run `./deploy.sh`
{{/eq}}
{{#eq testing "none"}}
5. Archive `node_modules`
6. Build (`npm run build`)
7. Archive `dist/`
8. SCP build to EC2 `~/builds`
9. SCP node_modules to EC2 `~/modules`
10. SSH into EC2 and run `./deploy.sh`
{{/eq}}

### Required GitHub Secrets

Go to **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions** and add:

| Secret | Description |
|---|---|
| `HOST` | EC2 public IP or hostname |
| `USER` | SSH username (e.g. `ubuntu`) |
| `KEY` | Private SSH key (contents of `.pem` file) |

